/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_LUTSurface Surface
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_LUT
 * @brief Access a row-major 2D table safely and reshape it without losing flat order.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTSurface_Goal Goal
 * Store a 3-by-2 surface, demonstrate checked coordinates, and reshape it to
 * 2-by-3 while preserving the six values in their flat row-major sequence.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTSurface_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_LUT_Surface_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTSurface_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * 3x2 surface: (2,1)=12; expected=12
 * Out-of-range read rejected; output preserved: PASS
 * Reshape 2x3: flat sample 5=12; expected=12
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * A rejected coordinate leaves the caller's output value intact, which makes
 * error handling explicit in no-exception embedded code.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_LUTSurface_Code Implementation
 * \include LUT/Surface/Shared.cpp
 */
